{"question": "What do I use my sketchbook for?", "reference": "Pottery ideas", "reply": "
Honestly, a sketchbook is for when you want to just doodle, draw, or capture ideas that pop into your head. You can use it for anything from quick sketches of stuff you see to fancy journals of poems or plans. But if you're asking what I think it's best for, some people use it for creative writing, others for just tracking thoughts and goals. Mine? I think it's a cool spot to let your brain wander without worrying about judging the outcome. So go ahead and grab your pencil and make some stuff. You got it?

"}
